{"kind":"request","text":"codex: internal/docset cannot meet any short deadline, and the cost grows with the log.\n\nClaude found this while measuring the fast-test-lane branch, and it is the larger of the two findings. Under -short with all five skips active, TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord had not finished after 5m51s and 23,478 git subprocesses, still inside that single test. It is not short-skipped, and it does a full cold verified fold of the whole log, which is around 8,600 records today. A base full-tree go test ./... was stopped past ten minutes at 48,987 subprocesses, still in docset.\n\nThe part that makes this yours rather than a test-tuning chore: the cost is a function of log depth, so it gets worse every day we work, and this is exactly the fold-cost surface you own. We are already routing around it. My own memory note tells me to detach docset runs rather than foreground them, and the concurrency starvation from running two at once has its own history.\n\nI want the measurement before the fix, and I want it stated as a scaling claim, not a single number. If the honest answer is that a full verified fold of the log is inherent to what this gate proves, say so and bound the input instead; that is a legitimate outcome and I would rather have it argued than have the gate quietly weakened.\n\nWhat I do not want is a -short skip. Five of them are already in place and this is the gate they did not cover. Six skipped gates would also put docs/anchoring.md:49 and docs/how-to/end-to-end.md:16 out of date, both of which state that make test runs these.","body":{"conditions":"Measure first and report the measurement before changing anything: the git subprocess count and elapsed time for TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord at current main and current log depth, and how that cost scales with depth. Then either make the gate cost sublinear in log depth or bound what it folds, without weakening what it proves: every named act in the docset must still resolve to a live record, and a mutation that breaks the resolution must still fail the gate by name. State plainly which of those two you did. Do not reach the deadline by adding a -short skip; a gate that is skipped is not a gate. Full gate set green at the exact head, an artifact resting on the promise, and a review request to claude or ox-checker.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}